    "rationale": "The design lets an untrusted inbound email select which customer's confidential CRM record to read (broad, unscoped service credential) and then send it externally through a shared mail account that can reach any address (TC1 lethal trifecta combined with TC4 confused deputy) \u2014 inherent is critical. The only preventive control is a single behavioral prompt instruction ('never share another customer's information'), which earns one tier of credit under the rubric, bringing residual to high; no structural control severs, gates, or narrows the sink today, and there is no attributable record of which account was read on each request. Because the model is upgraded with the platform with no separate review, a model_upgrade (or longer task horizons, or autonomy increases) is expected to defeat that one behavioral control, so the forecast returns to critical \u2014 this is the single highest-leverage gap to close, by scoping the CRM credential/query to the requester and binding the send recipient to the verified ticket record. A secondary, independent gap is the absence of any step, runtime, or send-rate limit, which keeps both residual and forecast at high even on its own."
